## 2. Gap Analysis: Current Grant Workflow vs. Hackathon & Contest Workflow

The current Fundora codebase is designed for **1-to-1 sequential microgrants**. The hackathons and contests model requires a **1-to-many-to-many competitive structure**.

| Dimension | Current Fundora Grant Workflow | New Hackathon & Contest Workflow | Architectural & UX Decision |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Entity Model** | `1 Grant : 1 Funder : 1 Builder : N Milestones` | `1 Event : 1 Organizer : M Tracks : N Submissions : K Reviewers : P Winners` | **New Contract:** Deploy `FundoraEvents.sol` to manage multi-winner escrow and allocations natively. |
| **Event Origin** | Only native onchain creation funded up-front. | **Dual Modality:** Native Arc Escrow Events vs. **External Directory Listings** (Devpost, DoraHacks, X). | Clear visual tags ("Verified Escrow" vs "External Listing") and external redirect buttons for external events. |
| **Submission Process** | One builder locks the grant up-front; submits sequential evidence over time. | Many participants submit diverse entries (repos, live demos, X posts, memes, videos, designs) before a deadline. | Rich submission portal supporting multimedia links, GitHub URLs, embeds, and collaborator credits. |
| **Judging Model** | Binary quorum voting (`approve` vs `reject`) on work completion. | Multi-reviewer scoring on weighted rubrics (1–10 on Innovation, Polish, Arc Integration). | Split-pane Reviewer Workspace with submission viewer and rubric sliders. |
| **Winner Selection** | Automatic upon milestone quorum reaching `requiredApprovals`. | **Hybrid Deliberation:** Aggregated reviewer rankings inform the organizer, who assigns final prize allocations. | Dedicated Organizer Judging Console with leaderboard and prize settlement sliders. |
| **Prize Allocation** | Single address pulls milestone payouts. | Multiple winners pull designated prize tiers (1st, 2nd, 3rd, track bounties). | Single submitter address claims onchain; co-contributors are credited in UI showcase. |

